  "modified_note": "modified=true entries carry deliberate board adaptations: slots.c/disk_activity.c match the PCIe switch downstream BDFs by domain-independent :c2:0X.0/ suffix (this board enumerates the switch in PCI domain 0003, the handoff assumed 0004); ix_thermal_runtime.c/ix_thermal_sampler.c use CLOCK_BOOTTIME so cache age cannot hide suspend time. worker.c: helper_exec no longer demands a read-only root (upstream ST_RDONLY); the equivalent integrity proof is the daemon-side SHA256 manifest verification, because this image ships a writable ext4 root. ix_power_runner.c: marker_and_worker no longer demands a read-only root (upstream ST_RDONLY on the marker and the worker binary); the equivalent integrity proof is the daemon-side manifest SHA256 verification. ix_power_runner.c: marker_and_worker opens bin/ without O_NOFOLLOW because Debian usrmerge makes /bin a symlink; the worker binary itself keeps the nofollow open and all checks. lab_consumers.c: an empty mountinfo is accepted when the scanned process lives in the scanner's own mount namespace (identical ns inode; chrooted base daemons such as avahi report empty mountinfo), because the caller's base observation already parsed that shared view; every other empty case still fails closed. lab_consumers.c: a successful zero-byte mountinfo read is treated as the kernel-attested empty mount list of that namespace (avahi chroot and dhcpcd unshared-ns base daemons report it); the fd scan still runs. ix_hold_state.c: record_valid pins the BDF domain to 3 (this board enumerates the switch in domain 0003; upstream assumed 0004); bridge identity is verified at runtime. y4_os_ix_hold_state.h/ix_hold_state.c: evidence bit 14 (PCC_OFF) introduced for the switch-native power model and the required HELD/ON evidence sets adapted to the provable signals of this carrier (no EN/PERST GPIOs; PCC changes with the power action)."
